5.5 Current-Thumbnail Highlight
===============================

The thumbnail at point is outlined with the
‘dired-video-thumbnail-current-thumbnail’ face, and the cursor is
recolored to match.  The outline is drawn inside the thumbnail, so
navigating never changes the thumbnail sizes or re-flows the grid.  Its
color follows the active theme's ‘highlight’ background unless the
face's ‘:box’ sets an explicit ‘:color’.

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-highlight-current-thumbnail
     Whether to outline the thumbnail at point.  Default: ‘t’.

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-highlight-cursor
     Whether to recolor the cursor to match the highlight,
     buffer-locally.  Default: ‘t’.

 -- Face: dired-video-thumbnail-current-thumbnail
     Face for the outline.  Customize the ‘:box’ ‘:line-width’ to change
     its thickness, or give it an explicit ‘:color’.

          (set-face-attribute 'dired-video-thumbnail-current-thumbnail nil
                              :box '(:line-width -5 :color "orange"))


File: dired-video-thumbnail.info,  Node: Sorting Settings,  Next: Per-Directory Settings,  Prev: Current-Thumbnail Highlight,  Up: Customization

