5.7 Per-Directory Settings
==========================

Sort order, filters and the thumbnail display height are remembered per
directory.  Changing them in a thumbnail buffer writes the choice into
that directory's ‘.dir-locals.el’ (under the nil class, merged with any
existing entries), and opening the directory restores it.  Only the
package's own variables are ever written.

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-save-dir-settings
     Whether to remember sort, filter and display-height choices per
     directory.  Default: ‘t’.  Set to ‘nil’ to keep such choices
     session-local.

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-default-filter
     Default name/duration/size filter, as a plist or ‘nil’ for no
     filter.  The plist has the form ‘(:name REGEXP :duration-min
     SECONDS :duration-max SECONDS :size-min BYTES :size-max BYTES)’,
     where each value may be ‘nil’.

          (setq dired-video-thumbnail-default-filter
                '(:name "holiday" :duration-min 30 :duration-max 600
                  :size-min 1048576 :size-max nil))

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-default-display-height
     Default thumbnail display height in pixels, or ‘nil’ for the global
     value.


File: dired-video-thumbnail.info,  Node: Recursive Settings,  Next: File Validation,  Prev: Per-Directory Settings,  Up: Customization

5.8 Recursive Settings
======================

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-recursive
     Whether to always search for videos recursively in subdirectories.
     Default: ‘nil’.

          (setq dired-video-thumbnail-recursive t)

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-auto-recursive
     Whether to automatically search recursively when no videos in
     current directory.  When non-‘nil’, if the current directory
     contains no video files but has subdirectories,
     ‘dired-video-thumbnail’ will automatically search recursively.
     This is useful for video collections organized in year/category
     folders.  Default: ‘t’.

          (setq dired-video-thumbnail-auto-recursive nil)


File: dired-video-thumbnail.info,  Node: File Validation,  Next: Confirmation,  Prev: Recursive Settings,  Up: Customization

5.9 File Validation
===================

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-minimum-file-size
     Minimum file size in bytes for a video to be included.  Files
     smaller than this are assumed to be corrupt or empty and are
     silently excluded.  Set to 0 to disable the check.  Default: ‘100’.

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-validate-headers
     Whether to verify each candidate file's first 12 bytes against
     known video container signatures (ISO BMFF/MP4/MOV/M4V/3GP,
     Matroska/WebM, AVI, FLV, Ogg, ASF/WMV and MPEG program/elementary
     streams).  Default: ‘nil’.


File: dired-video-thumbnail.info,  Node: Confirmation,  Next: Advanced Settings,  Prev: File Validation,  Up: Customization

5.10 Confirmation
=================

 -- User Option: dired-video-thumbnail-auto-accept
     Whether to skip confirmation for file actions like deletion and
     moving.  When non-‘nil’, deleting videos, creating a move target
     directory and overwriting an existing file proceed without
     prompting.  Default: ‘nil’.


